        30,
        180
      ],
      "sensor": "PPG (helmet/headband)",
      "desc": "Beats per minute. Spaceflight fluid shifts and deconditioning change resting HR; sustained tachycardia at rest can signal hypoxia, fever, hypoglycaemia or stress.",
      "source": "AHA adult resting HR 60-100 bpm; athletic crew may rest near 50 bpm.",
      "source_links": [
        [
          "AHA adult resting HR 60-100 bpm",
          "https://www.heart.org/en/health-topics/high-blood-pressure/the-facts-about-high-blood-pressure/all-about-heart-rate-pulse"
